"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. The surgical findings included a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) and pathological stage pT3a with extraprostatic extension, but favorable margins (negative) and no seminal vesicle invasion. The absence of lymph nodes removed and lymphovascular invasion was also noted. Preoperative PSA was 6.6. A key uncertainty is the missing biopsy grade and ISUP report, which widens the uncertainty regarding the true tumor characteristics. Furthermore, the lack of documented postoperative PSA or follow-up data prevents a definitive assessment of the subsequent trajectory. The status of nodal sampling is unknown, and the note confirms that pNx status does not equate to pN0, which increases uncertainty. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and their subsequent trend is crucial for revising this prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 43.46 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 26.08–60.84 months; its coverage has not been validated."
